## AI Agent Reasoning

### Context
The issue #92 diagnostic showed that disabling IndexedDB open after selecting a folder prevents Chrome from crashing when the tab closes.

### Decisions Made
- Persist handles immediately at folder open, reconnect, and save-to-folder boundaries.
- Use a startup gate that preserves workspace intent and coalesces edit state.
- Remove all asynchronous storage from beforeunload while retaining synchronous worker termination.
- Add a small lifecycle helper so the unload contract is directly testable.

### Trade-offs
- Very recent edits depend on a 300 ms proactive debounce instead of an unreliable unload write.
- Native FileSystemDirectoryHandle crash verification still requires manual testing in the affected Chrome profile.

